title: "CausalLayer MCP — Deterministic AI-Liability Attribution"
message: "If you use this software in research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "FaultKey Protocol"
    address: "Brisbane, Queensland, Australia"
    website: "https://faultkey.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/smq9sn5jck-coder/causallayer-mcp"
url: "https://faultkey.com"
abstract: >
  CausalLayer MCP is a Model Context Protocol server that issues signed,
  Bitcoin-anchored CausalCertificateV1 receipts attributing AI-incident
  liability between vendor, deployer, and end-user using a closed-form
  deterministic scoring function. Designed for AI insurance underwriting,
  APRA CPS 230 compliance, and EU AI Act Article 12 logging.
keywords:
  - "model context protocol"
  - "AI liability"
  - "AI governance"
  - "causal attribution"
  - "regtech"
  - "Ed25519"
  - "OpenTimestamps"
  - "deterministic AI"
